<BaseLayout title="Start Here — Where Is Baldo?" description="New here? This is where to start. The best posts, what this blog is about, and why a California barber has opinions about Albanian pizza.">

  <div class="post-header">
    <span class="post-tag">Start Here</span>
    <h1>New Here? Start Here.</h1>
    <p class="post-meta">The quick version of everything you need to know.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="post-body">

    <p>Welcome. You landed on a travel blog run by a barber from California who has been to 22 countries and has a compulsion to write about it. If you're wondering whether this is the right blog for you, here's the fast version:</p>

    <p><strong>This blog is for you if</strong> you want to travel to places that feel real. If you're tired of reading the same five "must-see" lists that all link to the same overpriced tourist experiences. If you travel on a budget and want stories from someone who actually does too — not someone who calls $200/night "budget" because they're comparing it to $400/night.</p>

    <p><strong>This blog is not for you if</strong> you want polished resort content, sponsored listicles, or travel writing that pretends everything is perfect all the time.</p>

    <h2>The Best Place to Start</h2>

    <p>If you're new, these are the posts that best capture what this blog is actually about:</p>

    <div class="start-cards">
      <a href="/blog/01-the-pizza-place-in-albania" class="start-card">
        <span class="start-card-emoji">🍕</span>
        <div>
          <strong>The Pizza Place in Albania</strong>
          <p>The story that explains why I travel the way I do. A random Tuesday in Vlore changed how I think about food, money, and getting lost on purpose.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/07-22-countries-10-things" class="start-card">
        <span class="start-card-emoji">🌍</span>
        <div>
          <strong>22 Countries, 10 Things I Actually Learned</strong>
          <p>Not a highlights reel. The actual lessons — including the ones that humbled me.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/09-how-i-travel-on-a-budget" class="start-card">
        <span class="start-card-emoji">💸</span>
        <div>
          <strong>How I Travel on a Budget (For Real)</strong>
          <p>Real numbers. Real strategies. From someone who has to make the math work because it's actual money, not an expense account.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/10-why-i-skip-tourist-areas" class="start-card">
        <span class="start-card-emoji">🚶</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Why I Always Skip the Tourist Areas</strong>
          <p>This is a principle, not a flex. Here's why it works and how to actually do it.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2>About Baldo</h2>

    <p>I'm Ubaldo — Baldo. California born, Mexican roots, no fixed address. I've been cutting hair for years and getting on planes for just as long. The two things go together better than you'd think — barbering is a portable skill, and barbershops are where real conversations happen.</p>

    <p>→ <a href="/about">Full story here</a></p>
    <p>→ <a href="/the-real-story">The real story here</a> (the longer, more honest version)</p>

    <h2>Follow Along</h2>

    <p>Instagram and TikTok: <strong>@whereisbaldo</strong></p>

    <p>If you want to support the blog without buying anything or clicking on ads (there aren't any), the best thing you can do is share a post that actually helped you. Or <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/whereisbaldo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">buy Baldo a taco</a>.</p>

    <p>Either way — glad you're here.</p>

    <p><em>— Baldo</em></p>

